--- stdout
Talk to an Iridium satellite handset over USB

[1m[4mUsage:[0m [1msatlink[0m [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

[1m[4mCommands:[0m
  [1mlist[0m     List connected handsets
  [1minfo[0m     Manufacturer, model, firmware and IMEI
  [1mstatus[0m   Signal strength, battery and network registration
  [1msms[0m      SMS operations
  [1mdial[0m     Place a voice call
  [1manswer[0m   Answer an incoming call
  [1mhangup[0m   End the current call
  [1mat[0m       Send a raw AT command, e.g. `satlink at AT+CSQ`
  [1mmonitor[0m  Print unsolicited events (incoming SMS, RING, ...) until interrupted
  [1mnet[0m      Use a data call as an IP link that only this program can use
  [1mhelp[0m     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

[1m[4mOptions:[0m
  [1m-p[0m, [1m--port[0m <PORT>
          Serial device (auto-detected by USB vendor ID when omitted)
          
          [env: SATLINK_PORT=]

  [1m-b[0m, [1m--baud[0m <BAUD>
          [default: 19200]

      [1m--simulate[0m[=<SIMULATE>]
          Use a simulated handset instead of a real one, with Iridium's real timing (the default) or instant responses

          Possible values:
          - [1miridium[0m: Call setup, latency and throughput as measured on Iridium
          - [1minstant[0m: No delays: for quick experiments

  [1m-v[0m, [1m--verbose[0m...
          Log what the link is doing (-v), in more detail (-vv, -vvv)

  [1m-h[0m, [1m--help[0m
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  [1m-V[0m, [1m--version[0m
          Print version
